cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "FlyLab: a dual-scorecard virtual pharmacology bench on the Drosophila MaleCNS connectome"
message: >-
  Cite the connectome papers first (MaleCNS v1.0, FlyWire), then this software.
  Nothing in FlyLab is a measurement from a living animal.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "FlyLab contributors"
version: 0.5.0
date-released: "2026-09-19"
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/pinkysworld/FlyLab
url: https://github.com/pinkysworld/FlyLab
abstract: >-
  FlyLab maps a compound and a free concentration onto Hill occupancy of an
  insect receptor panel and its vertebrate counterpart panel at the same dose,
  converts the insect side through a fixed mechanism table into gain
  multipliers on transmitter classes of a named MaleCNS v1.0 connectome cut,
  runs a deterministic rate model or a Shiu-style leaky integrate-and-fire
  model over that cut, and exports one notebook JSON with a provenance block
  (version, git SHA, compound-library SHA-256, map identifiers, seeds). It adds
  connectome null models, a receptor-versus-circuit selectivity landscape,
  retrospective rank validation against published orderings, published
  resistance alleles as per-compound EC50 shifts, combination-effect null
  models and a set of pre-registered predictions. It is not a new connectome,
  not regulatory toxicology and not a source of live-animal data.
keywords:
  - connectomics
  - Drosophila melanogaster
  - in-silico pharmacology
  - receptor occupancy
  - insecticide selectivity
  - null models
  - reproducible research
  - 3Rs
identifiers:
  - type: other
    value: "Zenodo DOI to be minted on release"
    description: Archived release DOI (placeholder until the deposit exists)
references:
  - title: MaleCNS v1.0 whole adult male Drosophila CNS connectome
    type: article
    year: 2026
    notes: >-
      HHMI Janelia FlyEM, University of Cambridge, MRC LMB and Google Research.
      CC-BY 4.0. The netlist FlyLab patches; downloaded, never redistributed.
  - title: "Neuronal wiring diagram of an adult brain (FlyWire)"
    type: article
    year: 2024
    doi: 10.1038/s41586-024-07558-y
  - title: >-
      A leaky integrate-and-fire computational model based on the connectome of
      the entire adult Drosophila brain reveals insights into sensorimotor
      processing
    type: article
    year: 2024
    notes: Shiu, Sterne, Spiller et al., Nature 634. Source of the LIF parameters and the bitter-veto direction used as a control.
